SupraLINUX Attica packaging notes
=================================

This Debian packaging targets KDE Frameworks Attica 6.30.0 for Ubuntu
Resolute as the SupraLINUX platform.

Authority and provider
----------------------

KDE upstream v6.30.0 defines the source, build requirements, SOVERSION and
default build behaviour. Ubuntu Resolute is a provider/compatibility target;
it does not select the KDE version.

Symbols baseline
----------------

The first Attica package proof deliberately starts from the exact Ubuntu
Resolute libkf6attica6 symbols baseline retained by the project's packaging
reference workflow. The large symbols file is injected by
scripts/run-kde-attica-package-preflight.sh before the source package is
created.

The retained baseline has SHA-256:

e67d131171c8e3ea79c6bbbb2434aa2492580d19ba7dccdaa7038766cd9827ad

The generated .dsc/.debian.tar.xz retained as build evidence contains the
actual libkf6attica6.symbols file used by dpkg-gensymbols. Any ABI delta in
KDE 6.30 must therefore be observed and reviewed rather than hidden.

Tests
-----

BUILD_TESTING remains enabled. The long-standing Debian-family patch disables
only providertest.cpp because Attica 6.30 still performs live network requests
to autoconfig.kde.org in that test. The other upstream autotests remain active.
REUSE-based outbound-license tests remain enabled when the build dependency is
available (it is an explicit Build-Depends here).

QDoc
----

Attica 6.30 uses ECMGenerateQDoc, where documentation generation is exposed
through explicit prepare/generate/QCH targets and is not part of the normal
build. The inherited BUILD_QCH=ON distro flag is therefore not used. The
libkf6attica-doc package name is retained for Debian/Ubuntu compatibility; a
separate documentation campaign can later decide whether to invoke the
explicit upstream QDoc targets across Frameworks consistently.
